{title: Because He Lives}
{key: G}
{x_theme: victory, healing, joy, easter}
{x_source: chrd:because_he_lives.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[G]Because He lives[G7], I can face [C]tomorrow,
Because He [G]lives, all fear is [D]gone;
Because I [G]kn   [C] -    [G]ow He holds the [C]future,
And life is [G]worth the living,
[D]Just because He [G]lives!

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]God sent His son, they called Him, [C]Jesus;
He came to [G]love, heal and [D]forgive;[D7]
He lived and [G]died [G7]to buy my [C]pardon,
An empty [G]grave is there to [D]prove my Savior [G]lives!

{comment: Verse 2}
[G]How sweet to hold a newborn [C]baby,
And feel the [G]pride and joy he [D]gives[D7];
But greater [G]still [G7]the calm as[C]surance:
This child can [G]face uncertain [D]days because He [G]Lives!

{comment: Verse 3}
[E]And then one [A]day, I'll cross the [D]river,
I'll fight life's [A]final war with [E]pain;[E7]
And then, as [A]death [A7]gives way to [D]victory,
